    "why_ka": {
      "type": "why-ka",
      "settings": {
        "heading": "Many languages. One first sound.",
        "body": "<p>South Asia's languages aren't dialects of one another. Many come from entirely different families, with their own scripts and their own histories.</p><p>But nearly every one of them teaches the alphabet the same way. The vowels come first, then the consonants: <em>ka, kha, ga, gha</em>. For most of us, <em>ka</em> was the first letter we ever learned.</p><p>So we named the company after the sound we all started with. It's the ring around the cup in our logo, and the letters running down the side of this page.</p>",
        "show_glyphs": false,
        "glyph_alt": "The letter ka, written in thirteen South Asian scripts",
        "caption": "\"Ka\", in thirteen South Asian scripts. The same sound, and almost nothing in common.",
        "closing": "A South Asian company, built for everyone. All of us.",
        "color_scheme": "scheme-8",
        "section_width": "page-width",
        "padding-block-start": 80,
        "padding-block-end": 80,
        "show_pattern": true,
        "pattern_opacity": 45,
        "pattern_color": "#f7ebe7"
      }
    }
